    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0553" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg503"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Tyler.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 77.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 122, diplomatic series, of the 23d ultimo, and to commend your action in the
                    matter of the religious persecution in Hamadan.</p>
                <p>The Department learns with pleasure that the measures taken by the Sadr Azem for
                    the protection of American citizens residing in Hamadan have proved effectual,
                    and it confidently hopes that no further trouble will occur there.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
